<title>JAPAN: Toyota falls on disappointing Japan sales.</title>
<headline>Toyota falls on disappointing Japan sales.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Toyota Motor Corp dropped for the third consecutive day on Tuesday, as sentiment continued to be hurt by disappointing Japanese domestic car sales in July, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0405 GMT, the share price of the leading car maker was down 160 yen at 3,130 yen. Its volume was 2.681 million shares.  </p>
<p>On Friday, the Japan Automobile Dealers' Association said that domestic vehicle sales fell 10.1 percent in July from a year earlier. It was the fourth straight month in which sales had fallen on a year-on-year basis.</p>
</text>
